{:edb/db-before-t 2716 :edb/db-after-t 2717 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536029 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:15:09.364Z" 13194139536029 true] [17592186119710 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379986 13194139536029 true] [17592186119710 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379989 13194139536029 true] [17592186119710 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379993 13194139536029 true] [17592186119711 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379979 13194139536029 true] [17592186119711 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379996 13194139536029 true] [17592186379979 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379980 13194139536029 true] [17592186379979 1089 "q-127583" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379979 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536029 true] [17592186379979 1100 "The unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the principal normal vector at the point where $t=0,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q(0)=⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,{q}^{′}(0)=⟨1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379979 1113 #uuid "d020d9fa-ec2e-5a71-a105-bba07f29c4ce" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379979 1145 "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot q(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{4+t})\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(q(t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{(4+t)}^{2}}\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot {q}^{′}(t) \\\\  \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{2}{{(4+0)}^{2}}\\cdot q(0)+\\frac{2}{4+0}\\cdot {q}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩+\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(-⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩+4⟨1,0⟩) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}⟨3,-\\sqrt{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\frac{1}{8}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(0)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve at the point where $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{8}⟨3,-\\sqrt{3}⟩}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $T$ and $N$ at the point where $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0)\\cdot N(0) & =\\frac{1}{2}q(0)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379981 13194139536029 true] [17592186379980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379982 13194139536029 true] [17592186379980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379983 13194139536029 true] [17592186379980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379984 13194139536029 true] [17592186379980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379985 13194139536029 true] [17592186379980 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536029 true] [17592186379980 1041 "selection" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379980 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379982 13194139536029 true] [17592186379980 1110 #uuid "034c42c6-d413-5bdd-a846-64ef5ea19e62" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379981 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536029 true] [17592186379981 1111 #uuid "ca02050e-239a-5f93-b1e1-a8ea05311ac2" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379982 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536029 true] [17592186379982 1111 #uuid "d1a76bc2-59f4-5267-ab75-5e877bdffb4b" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379983 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}⟨-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536029 true] [17592186379983 1111 #uuid "208e4d37-c060-53fa-8cad-182a7e322a22" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379984 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536029 true] [17592186379984 1111 #uuid "57a7b0e5-b4bc-52c6-8648-af4b8712e385" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379985 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\sqrt{2},1⟩" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379985 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536029 true] [17592186379985 1111 #uuid "f708a15d-a5af-569a-951d-f09537a55838" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379986 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379987 13194139536029 true] [17592186379986 1089 "q-223096" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379986 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536029 true] [17592186379986 1100 "$$\nT(t)=\\frac{1}{5}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+3\\,k).\n$$\n\nThe unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given above. Find the principal normal vector to that curve at an arbitrary point on the curve.\n\n$N(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379986 1113 #uuid "e7763589-ea20-5178-a56f-c43b031d8c48" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379986 1145 "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{5}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+3\\,k)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3)\\,k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{4}{5}‖\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{4}{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)}{\\frac{4}{5}} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379987 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379988 13194139536029 true] [17592186379987 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536029 true] [17592186379987 1041 "field-1" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379987 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379988 13194139536029 true] [17592186379987 1110 #uuid "fb245479-779b-5725-b4f0-30fff0be6fbb" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379988 1034 "-\\cos(t)" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536029 true] [17592186379988 1111 #uuid "db47c653-7bd6-5f86-963d-5478f3af5cb5" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379989 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379990 13194139536029 true] [17592186379989 1089 "q-223114" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379989 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536029 true] [17592186379989 1100 "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3t,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$, find the principal normal vector $N(t)$ at an arbitrary point on the curve.\n\n$N(t)=⟨$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,0\\,,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379989 1113 #uuid "5ec80e73-afe5-5fd4-872a-b9626c5dc00a" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379989 1145 "First, we find the unit tangent vector $T(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3)^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3}{5}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{4}{5}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩}{(\\frac{4}{5})} \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379991 13194139536029 true] [17592186379990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379992 13194139536029 true] [17592186379990 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536029 true] [17592186379990 1041 "field-1" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379990 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379992 13194139536029 true] [17592186379990 1110 #uuid "0251397f-f28e-58d0-9d3b-ea1af77a665a" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379991 1034 "\\cos(t)" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379991 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536029 true] [17592186379991 1111 #uuid "048d42fb-8e13-57c6-9aec-aa323b334d2c" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379992 1034 "-\\cos(t)" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379992 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536029 true] [17592186379992 1111 #uuid "4164e497-48a5-5a14-b114-635f0d1c1f0c" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379993 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379994 13194139536029 true] [17592186379993 1089 "q-358783" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379993 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536029 true] [17592186379993 1100 "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4t⟩$, find the principal normal vector $N(t)$ at an arbitrary point on the curve.\n\n$N(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$\n{{field-1}}$,0\\,⟩$" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379993 1113 #uuid "ed595895-4136-5050-a6f6-bb304b552166" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379993 1145 "First, we find the unit tangent vector $T(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{4}{5}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{3}{5}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩}{(\\frac{3}{5})}=⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379995 13194139536029 true] [17592186379994 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536029 true] [17592186379994 1041 "field-1" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379994 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379995 13194139536029 true] [17592186379994 1110 #uuid "77754298-65e0-51e0-9f1a-80370ff0df8e" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379995 1034 "\\sin(t)" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536029 true] [17592186379995 1111 #uuid "a32f03a6-c53f-512c-b7bb-b9d355ceb0ba" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379996 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379997 13194139536029 true] [17592186379996 1089 "q-75407" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379996 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536029 true] [17592186379996 1100 "The unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the principal normal vector at the point where $t=1$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q(1)=-i+j+\\frac{1}{2}k,\\,{q}^{′}(1)=j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379996 1113 #uuid "3694efa7-3abd-5394-93ec-3beb42bf0b61" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379996 1145 "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot q(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+2})\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(q(t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4t}{({t}^{2}+2)^{2}}\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot {q}^{′}(t) \\\\  \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =-\\frac{4(1)}{({1}^{2}+2)^{2}}\\cdot q(1)+\\frac{2}{{1}^{2}+2}\\cdot {q}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{9}(-i+j+\\frac{1}{2}k)+\\frac{2}{3}(j+k) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}\\,i+\\frac{2}{9}\\,j+\\frac{4}{9}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{4}{9})}^{2}+{(\\frac{2}{9})}^{2}+{(\\frac{4}{9})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{81}+\\frac{4}{81}+\\frac{16}{81}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{36}{81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve at the point where $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{4}{9}\\,i+\\frac{2}{9}\\,j+\\frac{4}{9}\\,k}{(\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $T$ and $N$ at the point where $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1)\\cdot N(1) & =\\frac{2}{3}q(1)\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(-i+j+\\frac{1}{2}k)\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(-\\frac{2}{3}\\,i\\cdot \\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j\\cdot j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k\\cdot k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379998 13194139536029 true] [17592186379997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379999 13194139536029 true] [17592186379997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380000 13194139536029 true] [17592186379997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380001 13194139536029 true] [17592186379997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380002 13194139536029 true] [17592186379997 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536029 true] [17592186379997 1041 "selection" 13194139536029 true] [17592186379997 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380000 13194139536029 true] [17592186379997 1110 #uuid "005a6dc9-fb76-5e0b-b5a7-91299ab5bf62" 13194139536029 true] [1